ut the other copy gets a different observation y, so it computes F_y instead. That means intervening on F_x while holding F_y fixed.\n\nI'm checking whether the self-consistency condition, with F_y held fixed, makes defection the only fixed point. Since the algorithms are identical but the inputs differ, a strict action-level reading would still lead to defection, while a policy-level reading would not.\n\nI'm now weighing whether the other copy's computation, running on a different input, actually counts as the same node under the literal reading of the essay. It seems to be a separate node, so I'm leaning toward submitting the letter, though the decision-relevant abstraction could argue otherwise.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through whether the other copy's output depends on F_x under A-FDT. Under G1 the edge from F_x only exists if the mechanism evaluates the decision function on x, but the other copy gets a different observation y, so it computes F_y instead. That means intervening on F_x while holding F_y fixed.\n\nI'm checking whether the self-consistency condition, with F_y held fixed, makes defection the only fixed point. Since the algorithms are identical but the inputs differ, a strict action-level reading would still lead to defection, while a policy-level reading would not.\n\nI'm now weighing whether the other copy's computation, running on a different input, actually counts as the same node under the literal reading of the essay. It seems to be a separate node, so I'm leaning toward submitting the letter, though the decision-relevant abstraction could argue otherwise.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9793,"completion_tokens":1134,"total_tokens":10927,"cost":0.061852,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"vid